# Drizzle writes one JSON snapshot per migration plus a journal, so a single
# schema change rewrites hundreds of lines nobody reads. GitHub counts them in
# the PR's +/- headline, which is why migration PRs look several times their
# reviewable size. Marking them generated collapses them in the diff view (and
# keeps them out of the repo's language stats).
#
# The migration `.sql` files stay visible on purpose: reviewers must read the
# DDL, and pr-check.yml's destructive-DDL gate greps
# `packages/db/src/migrations/*.sql` — non-recursive, so it never saw `meta/`.
packages/db/src/migrations/meta/** linguist-generated=true
